.","ts":546}],"comment":"Development is equal: both sides have spent two moves and developed one piece and one pawn each.","ts":538},{"id":"n18","san":"exf6","uci":"e7f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1n1ppp/2p2p2/8/3P4/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]}],"comment":"Forced: if White doesn't take on f6, Black takes on e4.","ts":505},{"id":"n19","san":"Bd3","uci":"f1d3","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/3B1N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 4 6","children":[{"id":"n20","san":"Nxe4","uci":"f6e4","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/2p5/8/3Pn3/3B1N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 7","children":[{"id":"n21","san":"Bxe4","uci":"d3e4","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/2p5/8/3PB3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 0 7","children":[{"id":"n22","san":"Nf6","uci":"d7f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PB3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 1 8","children":[],"comment":"Ndf6 hits the bishop on e4, and Black gains a tempo.","ts":529},{"id":"n23","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npp1p/2p3p1/8/3PB3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 8","children":[]},{"id":"n24","san":"a6","uci":"a7a6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/1p1npppp/p1p5/8/3PB3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 8","children":[]},{"id":"n25","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"r1b1kb1r/ppqnpppp/2p5/8/3PB3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 1 8","children":[]},{"id":"n26","san":"Qb6","uci":"d8b6","fen":"r1b1kb1r/pp1npppp/1qp5/8/3PB3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 1 8","children":[]},{"id":"n27","san":"a5","uci":"a7a5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/1p1npppp/2p5/p7/3PB3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 8","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"n28","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"r1b1kb1r/ppqnpppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/3B1N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 5 7","children":[]},{"id":"n29","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npp1p/2p2np1/8/3PN3/3B1N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]}],"comment":"Say White defends with Bd3 instead of taking. Black takes on e4, and after Bxe4 the d7 knight comes to f6 with tempo on the bishop.","ts":521}],"comment":"Black continues with Ngf6, and now White is forced to capture.","ts":505},{"id":"n30","san":"Ndf6","uci":"d7f6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 3 6","children":[]},{"id":"n31","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp1npp1p/2p3p1/8/3PN3/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 6","children":[]}]},{"id":"n32","san":"Ng5","uci":"e4g5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp1npppp/2p5/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 2 5","children":[{"id":"n33","san":"Ngf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 3 6","children":[{"id":"n34","san":"Bd3","uci":"f1d3","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/6N1/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 4 6","children":[{"id":"n35","san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1n1ppp/2p1pn2/6N1/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[],"comment":"White stands a bit better, but Black has compensation for White's lost tempi. Chasing the knight with h6 is okay, but it doesn't have to be played yet: White doesn't have many threats.","ts":612},{"id":"n36","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npp1p/2p2np1/6N1/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]},{"id":"n37","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"r1b1kb1r/ppqnpppp/2p2n2/6N1/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 5 7","children":[]},{"id":"n38","san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1n1ppp/2p2n2/4p1N1/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]},{"id":"n39","san":"Nb6","uci":"d7b6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/1np2n2/6N1/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 5 7","children":[]}]}],"comment":"The best move, and the most commonly played.","ts":604},{"id":"n40","san":"h6","uci":"h7h6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp1nppp1/2p4p/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[]},{"id":"n41","san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp1n1ppp/2p1p3/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[]},{"id":"n42","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"r1b1kbnr/ppqnpppp/2p5/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 3 6","children":[]},{"id":"n43","san":"Ndf6","uci":"d7f6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p2n2/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 3 6","children":[]}],"comment":"Ng5 strikes at f7 immediately, so Black has to be a little careful.","ts":587},{"id":"n44","san":"Qe2","uci":"d1e2","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp1npppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR b KQkq - 2 5","children":[{"id":"n45","san":"Ndf6","uci":"d7f6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 3 6","children":[{"id":"n46","san":"Nxf6+","uci":"e4f6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p2N2/8/3P4/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR b KQkq - 0 6","children":[{"id":"n47","san":"Nxf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3P4/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[],"comment":"Black recaptures on f6 and is safe.","ts":645},{"id":"n48","san":"gxf6","uci":"g7f6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/8/3P4/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]}]}],"comment":"Bring the d7 knight to f6, so that if White takes, you recapture and the d-file opens for your queen. Playing e6 to give the king a square, so the bishop covers d6, also works.","ts":645},{"id":"n49","san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp1n1ppp/2p1p3/8/3PN3/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[],"comment":"The other safe option: the king gets a square and the bishop can capture on d6. Both work; here, play the knight move.","ts":653},{"id":"n50","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"r1b1kbnr/ppqnpppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 3 6","children":[]},{"id":"n51","san":"Nb6","uci":"d7b6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/1np5/8/3PN3/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 3 6","children":[]},{"id":"n52","san":"Ngf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP1QPPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 3 6","children":[],"comment":"Developing normally loses at once: Nd6 is checkmate. The knight can't be taken and the king has no moves.","nags":[4],"ts":637}],"comment":"A scary idea you have to remember: Qe2 sets up a mate.","ts":628}],"comment":"The Karpov Variation. Black doesn't challenge the e4 knight yet: he prepares Ngf6 so he can recapture with the other knight, and the bishop stays on c8, where h4 and h5 can't chase it.","ts":471},{"id":"n53","san":"Bf5","uci":"c8f5","fen":"rn1qkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/5b2/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5","children":[],"comment":"The main line, also good. This chapter is about the Karpov: find the knight move.","ts":463},{"id":"n54","san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5","children":[]},{"id":"n55","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pp1p/2p3p1/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]},{"id":"n56","san":"h6","uci":"h7h6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2ppp1/2p4p/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]},{"id":"n57","san":"a5","uci":"a7a5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/1p2pppp/2p5/p7/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]}],"intro":"Back to move four, after Nxe4. Bf5 was the main move, but Black has two more very good options that give even more activity.","introTs":447,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c6","uci":"c7c6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 1 3"},{"san":"dxe4","uci":"d5e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3Pp3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nxe4","uci":"c3e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4"}]},{"id":"chapter-4","name":"4...Nf6: the Korchnoi Variation","url":"","annotator":null,"orientation":"black","startFen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4","gamebook":false,"moves":[{"id":"n0","san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5","children":[{"id":"n1","san":"Nxf6+","uci":"e4f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2N2/8/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 5","children":[{"id":"n2","san":"exf6","uci":"e7f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/2p2p2/8/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[{"id":"n3","san":"c3","uci":"c2c3","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/2p2p2/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 6","children":[{"id":"n4","san":"Bd6","uci":"f8d6","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp3ppp/2pb1p2/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7","children":[{"id":"n5","san":"Bd3","uci":"f1d3","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp3ppp/2pb1p2/8/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 2 7","children":[{"id":"n6","san":"O-O","uci":"e8g8","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp3ppp/2pb1p2/8/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQ - 3 8","children":[],"comment":"Both sides castle kingside and the middlegame is equal, if slightly boring. The catch: any endgame is unfavorable for Black because of the doubled f-pawns, a bit like the Berlin, where Black has no kingside pawn majority.","ts":726},{"id":"n7","san":"Nd7","uci":"b8d7","fen":"r1bqk2r/pp1n1ppp/2pb1p2/8/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 3 8","children":[]},{"id":"n8","san":"c5","uci":"c6c5","fen":"rnbqk2r/pp3ppp/3b1p2/2p5/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 8","children":[]},{"id":"n9","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"rnb1k2r/ppq2ppp/2pb1p2/8/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 3 8","children":[]},{"id":"n10","san":"Na6","uci":"b8a6","fen":"r1bqk2r/pp3ppp/n1pb1p2/8/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 3 8","children":[]}]}],"comment":"The most common plan: Black develops his bishops to d6 and e6.","ts":718},{"id":"n11","san":"Nd7","uci":"b8d7","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp1n1ppp/2p2p2/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7","children":[]},{"id":"n12","san":"a5","uci":"a7a5","fen":"rnbqkb1r/1p3ppp/2p2p2/p7/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]},{"id":"n13","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"rnb1kb1r/ppq2ppp/2p2p2/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7","children":[]},{"id":"n14","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp3p1p/2p2pp1/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]}],"comment":"White sets up with c3, Bd3, a knight to f3 and kingside castling.","ts":718}],"comment":"Taking with the e-pawn is the Korchnoi Variation. It's a very drawish line that doesn't give much counterplay.","ts":710},{"id":"n15","san":"gxf6","uci":"g7f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/8/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[],"comment":"The Bronstein-Larsen. Stjepan says it gives Black a lot of initiative but White is supposed to be positionally better, and the engine rates it a clear step down from exf6. The last chapter shows how it goes. Here, take with the e-pawn.","nags":[6],"ts":751}],"comment":"White has to capture: if he lets the knight be challenged, it just goes back with tempo.","ts":694}],"comment":"The second most popular continuation. It branches into two variations.","ts":678},{"id":"n16","san":"Nd7","uci":"b8d7","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp1npppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5","children":[],"comment":"4...Nd7, the Karpov, is also good. This chapter is about ...Nf6.","ts":678},{"id":"n17","san":"Bf5","uci":"c8f5","fen":"rn1qkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/5b2/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5","children":[],"comment":"The main line, also good. This chapter is about the knight move that challenges e4.","ts":678},{"id":"n18","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pp1p/2p3p1/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]},{"id":"n19","san":"h6","uci":"h7h6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2ppp1/2p4p/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]},{"id":"n20","san":"a5","uci":"a7a5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/1p2pppp/2p5/p7/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]}],"intro":"One more line after Nxe4 that isn't Bf5 or the Karpov: challenge the knight with your own.","introTs":670,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c6","uci":"c7c6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 1 3"},{"san":"dxe4","uci":"d5e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3Pp3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nxe4","uci":"c3e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4"}]},{"id":"chapter-5","name":"If you choose the Bronstein-Larsen","url":"","annotator":null,"orientation":"black","startFen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/8/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6","gamebook":false,"moves":[{"id":"n0","san":"c3","uci":"c2c3","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 6","children":[{"id":"n1","san":"Bf5","uci":"c8f5","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/5b2/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7","children":[{"id":"n2","san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/5b2/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 2 7","children":[{"id":"n3","san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp3p1p/2p1pp2/5b2/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 8","children":[],"comment":"Black has a lot of activity with the bishop pair. The plan is to castle queenside and put a rook on g8 to strike down the g-file, so White will have a hard time castling kingside. In any endgame, though, Black is slightly worse because of the ruined kingside structure.","ts":776},{"id":"n4","san":"Nd7","uci":"b8d7","fen":"r2qkb1r/pp1npp1p/2p2p2/5b2/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 3 8","children":[]},{"id":"n5","san":"Bg6","uci":"f5g6","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2pb1/8/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 3 8","children":[]},{"id":"n6","san":"h5","uci":"h7h5","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp2pp2/2p2p2/5b1p/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 8","children":[]},{"id":"n7","san":"a5","uci":"a7a5","fen":"rn1qkb1r/1p2pp1p/2p2p2/p4b2/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 8","children":[]}]}],"comment":"Black develops the bishop to f5, and both sides keep developing.","ts":768},{"id":"n8","san":"Qd5","uci":"d8d5","fen":"rnb1kb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/3q4/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7","children":[]},{"id":"n9","san":"h5","uci":"h7h5","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pp2/2p2p2/7p/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]},{"id":"n10","san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp3p1p/2p2p2/4p3/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 7","children":[]},{"id":"n11","san":"Na6","uci":"b8a6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pp1p/n1p2p2/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7","children":[]},{"id":"n12","san":"Qd6","uci":"d8d6","fen":"rnb1kb1r/pp2pp1p/2pq1p2/8/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 7","children":[]}]}],"intro":"Recapturing with the g-pawn is the Bronstein-Larsen. Stjepan warns that White is supposed to be positionally and strategically better, and the engine agrees, but Black gets a lot of initiative for the doubled pawns and the broken kingside.","introTs":751,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c6","uci":"c7c6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 1 3"},{"san":"dxe4","uci":"d5e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3Pp3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nxe4","uci":"c3e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4"},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5"},{"san":"Nxf6+","uci":"e4f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2N2/8/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 5"},{"san":"gxf6","uci":"g7f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pp1p/2p2p2/8/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6"}]}]}